  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3486c83b95be55d49b7e64a9a2619506, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::BookReader
  bookPanel: {fileID: 11221582}
  bookPrompt: {fileID: 886279709}
  titleText: {fileID: 710101721}
  storyText: {fileID: 1459113383}
  bookTitle: The Sleeping Crystal Castle
  story: 'Beyond the hills of Wonderland stood an ancient castle made of shining
    crystals.



    Long ago, the castle was filled with magic and laughter, but
    one day its lights slowly faded and the halls became silent.



    The people
    believed the castle was not abandoned, but waiting for a special visitor who
    could awaken its forgotten magic.



    Many explorers searched for the secret
    of the castle, but only those who followed their imagination could discover the
    hidden power inside.



    It was said that the castle never chose the strongest
    person, but the one who still believed in wonder.'
